IS_SESSION_LOG FILENAME RULE (src/provider.rs) — must be EXACT-name, and must never match the transient temp files that safeWriteJson creates:
  Provider::RooCode => matches!(lower_filename.as_str(), "ui_messages.json" | "history_item.json"),
  Excluded on purpose: "_index.json" (flat index), "api_conversation_history.json" (raw conversation — Discodex must never open it), "task_metadata.json", and every ".ui_messages.json.new_*.tmp" / ".ui_messages.json.bak_*.tmp" (leading dot + .tmp suffix => exact match excludes them). Because both names match, recent_logs() would count 2 files per task — de-duplicate by parent directory for RooCode so the "newest N" limit counts TASKS, not files.

WATCHER CHANGES (src/watcher.rs) — LogTailer CANNOT be used (byte-offset cursor + newline splitting is invalid for an atomically-replaced single-line JSON array). Add a dedicated reader:
  pub struct RooTaskReader { emitted: HashMap<PathBuf, usize> }   // ui_messages.json path -> messages already emitted
  impl RooTaskReader {
      pub fn read_task(&mut self, task_dir: &Path) -> io::Result<Vec<String>> {
          let mut lines = Vec::new();
          // 1. history_item.json: single object, always re-emit (idempotent SessionMetadata).
          if let Ok(raw) = fs::read_to_string(task_dir.join("history_item.json")) { lines.push(raw); }
          // 2. ui_messages.json: JSON array; emit only elements we have not seen.
          let msgs = task_dir.join("ui_messages.json");
          let arr: Vec<Value> = serde_json::from_str(&fs::read_to_string(&msgs)?).unwrap_or_default();
          let seen = self.emitted.entry(msgs.clone()).or_insert(0);
          if arr.len() < *seen { *seen = 0; }                       // file rewritten/shrunk
          for m in &arr[*seen..] { lines.push(serde_json::to_string(m)?); }   // one JSON object per line
          *seen = arr.len();
          Ok(lines)
      }
  }
  Caveat to handle: Task.say() MUTATES the last message in place on a partial->complete transition without changing its ts, so index-diffing alone would miss that final update. Fix cheaply by also re-emitting the last element when its `partial` flag flips true->false (store the previous value per task). Also cap the read size (skip files > ~64 MB) to avoid OOM on pathological tasks.

MAIN.RS CHANGES (src/main.rs):
  - The startup scan and the notify handler both call tailer.read_from_start()/read_new(). For RooCode, branch on the provider: `if source.provider == Provider::RooCode { roo_reader.read_task(path.parent()) } else { tailer.read_new(path) }`, and feed the resulting lines through the SAME apply_lines()/apply_historical_lines() helpers. This keeps the whole-file/one-object-per-line output flowing into parse_line_for unchanged.
  - apply_historical_lines() derives the per-event time via events::line_timestamp_ms(), which only looks at "timestamp"/"created_at"/"time"/"createdAt". Roo uses "ts". Add `.or_else(|| value.get("ts"))` to line_timestamp_ms() so historical replay is timestamped per message (safe: none of the other four providers use a top-level "ts" key).
  - The notify watcher already watches each source root recursively, so ui_messages.json and history_item.json changes both fire; the reader is directory-scoped and idempotent, so either trigger produces the same correct result.
  - No new dependency: serde_json is already used; no sqlite crate needed.

