FORMAT-CHURN RISK AND FAIL-SAFE:
  Risks: (1) Roo renames ui_messages.json/history_item.json; (2) the ClineMessage schema changes (new say/ask values, field renames); (3) the ClineSayTool `tool` token vocabulary changes; (4) the `tasks/<id>/` layout moves (e.g. a new storage engine); (5) safeWriteJson switches to a different write strategy (e.g. real append) so the file becomes newline-delimited; (6) the `customStoragePath` setting relocates the root; (7) a user-authored custom mode slug appears in `mode`.
  Fail safe: unknown tool tokens -> "Using development tools" (never echo the token, it could be user text); unknown ask/say values -> emit NOTHING (never forward unknown text); ui_messages.json that fails to parse as an array -> treat as empty, never fall back to line-splitting; never open api_conversation_history.json; read size cap; all reader errors are swallowed so the worker never dies; if the expected files disappear the provider silently degrades to the EXISTING focused-app detection (Provider::from_window already recognises "Roo Code" in a VS Code title) — the adapter is strictly additive and cannot regress the current behaviour.
